cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it, and read DISCLAIMER.md before using any
  output: this is research software, not a validated diagnostic assay, no threshold in
  packs/*/pack.yaml is a measured operating point, and nothing it produces should be used
  to decide that a sample is safe. The published databases are derived data - a dated
  snapshot of public NCBI records - and are out of date by design.
title: bioThreatFinder
abstract: >-
  A Nextflow pipeline for metagenomic screening and in-silico confirmation of
  high-consequence pathogens across human, animal and plant health. A permissive
  stage-1 screen across multiple classifier arms feeds a strict, per-candidate
  stage 2 that maps reads against each target together with its near neighbours,
  so reads preferring a harmless relative are attributed to the relative rather
  than to the watchlist taxon. A marker-gene tier gates the top evidence tier
  where the chromosome is not the actionable signal.
type: software
version: 0.4.0
date-released: '2026-10-23'
